 "capsule": "Following the 25 April 1974 Carnation Revolution that ended the Estado Novo dictatorship, Portugal adopted a new democratic constitution in April 1976 establishing a semi-presidential parliamentary republic and completing the rapid decolonization of its African territories. It joined the European Communities in 1986 and adopted the euro in 1999-2002, with alternating Socialist and Social Democratic governments steering the country through the 2011 sovereign-debt bailout and its recovery into the 2020s.",
